  "comment": "**What it does**\n**Earnings momentum** - analysts keep raising their numbers, and the company keeps beating them. The research calls estimate revisions one of the strongest forward return signals there is.\n\n- **Upgrades in progress** - consensus EPS raised 7%+ over BOTH the last month and the last 3 months.\n- **Broad agreement** - more analysts raising than cutting.\n- **A habit of beating** - beat in at least 3 of the last 4 quarters, with a positive average surprise. This is the post-earnings-drift effect: positive surprises keep paying for weeks or months.\n- **Trustworthy** - at least 3 analysts covering.\n- **Confirmation** - above the 200-day line, daily moves under 5.5%.\n\n**One choice you made**: your blocks as literally written ('raised' = any uptick) returned **639** names, far past the ~30-200 you wanted. You chose to define 'raised' as a **meaningful 7%+ upgrade**, which gives **165** and leaves your 'beat 3 of 4 quarters' rule exactly as written.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- **The revision size is the main dial.** 3% gives ~334, 5% gives ~233, 7% gives ~165, 10% gives ~112.\n- **Want the very best?** Require `earnings_beat_rate = 100` (beat all four quarters). At 7% that gives ~113.\n- **Want a wider net?** Drop both revision blocks to 3%.\n- **Note**: the 3-month window contains the 1-month window, so requiring both is a test of *sustained* upgrading, not two independent signals.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `momentum_score`** - the market acting on the upgrades.\n- **Tiebreak on `eps_revision_1m`** - the freshest upgrade, and the sharpest edge of the signal.\n- **Avoid `value_score`** - names being upgraded are rarely cheap, so it fights the thesis.\n- **Worth a look**: sort by `days_to_next_earnings` ascending to see which names report soonest - that is a timing risk, not a quality measure.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find stocks where the analysts keep raising their numbers \u2014 the earnings-momentum\nscreen (revisions plus a habit of beating estimates).\n- **Goal**: earnings momentum. **Dividends**: ignore.\n- **Upgrades in progress**: consensus EPS estimate raised over BOTH the last month\n  and the last 3 months, with more analysts raising than cutting.\n- **A habit of beating**: beat estimates in at least 3 of the last 4 quarters,\n  positive average surprise.\n- **Trustworthy**: at least 3 analysts. **Confirmation**: above the 200-day line.\n- **Size**: $500M and bigger. **Kinds**: normal stocks, banks, insurance and REITs.\n- **Risk**: moderate. **Results**: ~30-200 names.\n- **Sorting**: momentum first, tiebreak the 1-month EPS revision itself.",
